Feature: TC_06_STAFF - BISS Letters Coordination Amendment E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Suite for BISS Letters" (BISSAGL-7301, AT-TC-01 and 02, tmslinks BISSAGL-14914 / 14913)
  # Rewritten 16-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary (the wording the MAPS features run with).
  #
  # Purpose:
  #   2023 BISS letters must be issued in the name of the previous herd owner after a herd change. The setup for that
  #   check is a coordination amendment: every parcel of the application is moved to the new herd U1222127 and saved.
  #
  # Legacy coverage notes carried forward:
  #   - AT-TC-01 and AT-TC-02 were the same steps on the same data (only the tmslink differed); run once here.
  #   - Legacy took "Reference Number from row 2" while its AT-TC-00 loaded Admin Check Not Started herds; the
  #     reference number pool is used here, as the search step needs a reference number.
  #   - Legacy only clicked Save. Here Save must not show a form error, and the confirmation message is logged.
  #
  # Data warning:
  #   This moves ALL parcels of a CENTEST application to herd U1222127 and does not move them back (legacy had no
  #   reset either). CENTEST is a copy of production, so pick the run with the test owner.
  #
  # Test data:
  #   Reference number from the database ("Get Reference Numbers", scheme year 2023). New herd U1222127 (legacy literal).
  #   Login agr4442 (BISS Co-ordination 1). Password: TD:Password from the TestData row of this test case.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps (Correspondence - coordination amendments)
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Background:
    Given the staff user is logged in to the BISS internal portal as "agr4442"

  @regression @staff @letters @coordination @e2e
  Scenario: AT-STAFF-LETTERS-E2E-01 - Staff moves all parcels of an application to a new herd through Coordination Amendments

    # SECTION 1 : Move all parcels to the new herd - AT-TC-01 (BISSAGL-14914) / AT-TC-02 (BISSAGL-14913)
    When the staff user opens the application for the next reference number for scheme year "2023"
    And the staff user starts a coordination amendment to herd "U1222127"
    And the staff user moves all parcels to the new herd
    Then the coordination amendment should be saved
